<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3691" root="تأر" body-key="t">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَرَّةٌ</span></b> : (Msb, K:) or <i>a time, whether long or short;</i>
syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حِينٌ</span>: (IAar:) sometimes, however, it is
pronounced <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَأْرَةٌ</span>: (Msb:) pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تِئَرٌ</span> (T, Msb, K)
and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تِئَارٌ</span>: (Msb:) these are pls. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَأْرَةٌ</span>; but the
pl. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَارَةٌ</span> without <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ء</span> is <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَارَاتٌ</span> (Msb) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تِيَرٌ</span> (S in
art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تير</span>, and K and K in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تور</span>,) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تِيَارٌ</span>. (S in art.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تير</span>.) [See also art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تور</span>.]

